   </table><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:9pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><span style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:9pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</span></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Adjusted net income and adjusted diluted earnings per share (&#8220;EPS&#8221;) are non-GAAP financial measures. These non-GAAP financial measures exclude net gains and losses from investments in OpenAI. Refer to the Non-GAAP Financial Measures section of our fiscal year 2026 Form 10-K for a reconciliation of our financial results reported in accordance with GAAP to non-GAAP financial results.</span></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:13.5pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-style:italic;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Fiscal Year 2026 Compared with Fiscal Year 2025</span></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:9pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Revenue increased $50.1 billion or 18% driven by growth in Agents and Infra. Agents and Infra revenue increased driven by Azure and Microsoft 365 commercial cloud. Devices and Consumer revenue increased driven by Search and advertising, offset in part by a decline in XBOX.</span></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:9pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Cost of revenue increased $18.5 billion or 21% driven by growth in Agents and Infra.</span></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:9pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Gross margin increased $31.6 billion or 16% with growth across both of our segments.</span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> </span></p><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="margin-left:5.731%;tab-size:32px;display:flex;font-size:10pt;margin-top:4.5pt;justify-content:flex-start;font-family:Arial;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;min-width:3.333%;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:3.5356267702001714%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#8226;</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Gross margin percentage decreased slightly driven by continued investments in AI infrastructure and growing AI product usage, offset in part by efficiency gains across the Microsoft Cloud.</span></div></div><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="margin-left:5.731%;tab-size:32px;display:flex;font-size:10pt;margin-top:4.5pt;justify-content:flex-start;font-family:Arial;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;min-width:3.333%;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:3.5356267702001714%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#8226;</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Microsoft Cloud gross margin percentage decreased to 66% driven by continued investments in AI infrastructure and growing AI product usage, offset in part by efficiency gains in Azure and Microsoft 365 commercial cloud.</span></div></div><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:9pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Operating expenses increased $4.9 billion or 7% driven by continued investments in research and development compute capacity, AI talent, and data to support product development that benefits the entire portfolio, impairment and other related expenses in our XBOX business, investments in commercial sales, and higher Copilot advertising expenses.</span></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:9pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Operating income increased $26.7 billion or 21% with growth across both of our segments.</span></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:9pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Revenue and operating income both included a favorable foreign currency impact of 2%.</span></p></div>
  <div style="z-index:2;flex-direction:column;display:flex;padding-bottom:0.4in;min-height:0.6in;justify-content:flex-end;position:relative;box-sizing:border-box;"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:8pt;margin-top:12pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:center;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:8pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">11</span></p></div>
  <hr style="margin-inline-start:auto;margin-inline-end:auto;page-break-after:always;"/>
  <div style="padding-top:0.5in;z-index:2;min-height:0.6in;position:relative;box-sizing:border-box;"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:7.5pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:center;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;text-decoration:underline solid;font-size:7.5pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">PART II</span></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:7.5pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:center;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:7.5pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Item 7</span></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:9pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:center;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;"><span style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:9pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</span></p></div>
  <div class="main-content-container" style="z-index:5;position:relative;"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:9pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Fiscal year 2026 net income and diluted EPS were positively impacted by net gains from investments in OpenAI, which resulted in an increase in net income and diluted EPS of $5.0 billion and $0.67, respectively. Fiscal year 2025 net income and diluted EPS were negatively impacted by net losses from investments in OpenAI, which resulted in a decrease in net income and diluted EPS of $3.6 billion and $0.49, respectively.</span></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:13.5pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-style:italic;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Fiscal Year 2025 Compared with Fiscal Year 2024</span></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:9pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Revenue increased $36.6 billion or 15% driven by growth in Agents and Infra. Agents and Infra revenue increased driven by Azure and Microsoft 365 commercial cloud. Devices and Consumer revenue increased driven by Search and advertising and XBOX.</span></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:9pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Cost of revenue increased $13.7 billion or 19% driven by growth in Agents and Infra.</span></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:9pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Gross margin increased $22.9 billion or 13% with growth across both of our segments.</span></p><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="margin-left:5.731%;tab-size:32px;display:flex;font-size:10pt;margin-top:4.5pt;justify-content:flex-start;font-family:Arial;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;min-width:3.333%;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:3.5356267702001714%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#8226;</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Gross margin percentage decreased slightly driven by Agents and Infra, offset in part by Devices and Consumer.</span></div></div><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="margin-left:5.731%;tab-size:32px;display:flex;font-size:10pt;margin-top:4.5pt;justify-content:flex-start;font-family:Arial;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;min-width:3.333%;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:3.5356267702001714%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#8226;</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Microsoft Cloud gross margin percentage decreased to 69% driven by the impact of scaling our AI infrastructure, offset in part by efficiency gains in Azure.</span></div></div><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:9pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Operating expenses increased $3.8 billion or 6% driven by investments in cloud and AI engineering and XBOX, including the impact of the Activision Blizzard acquisition.</span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> </span></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:9pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Operating income increased $19.1 billion or 17% with growth across both of our segments.</span></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:13.5pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:center;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;text-decoration:underline solid;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">SEGMENT RESULTS OF OPERATIONS</span></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:9pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><span style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:9pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</span></p>
