  <div style="padding-top:0.5in;z-index:2;min-height:0.6in;position:relative;box-sizing:border-box;"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:7.5pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:center;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;text-decoration:underline solid;font-size:7.5pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">PART II</span></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:7.5pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:center;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:7.5pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Item 7</span></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:9pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:center;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;"><span style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:9pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</span></p></div>
  <div class="main-content-container" style="z-index:5;position:relative;"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:4.5pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Reportable Segments</span></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:9pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-style:italic;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Fiscal Year 2026 Compared with Fiscal Year 2025</span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-style:italic;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> </span></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:9pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-style:italic;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Agents and Infra</span></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:9pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Revenue increased $49.3 billion or 23%.</span></p><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="margin-left:5.731%;tab-size:32px;display:flex;font-size:10pt;margin-top:4.5pt;justify-content:flex-start;font-family:Arial;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;min-width:3.333%;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:3.5356267702001714%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#8226;</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Azure revenue increased $29.3 billion or 40% driven by demand for services across the platform with continued growth across all workloads. </span></div></div><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="margin-left:5.731%;tab-size:32px;display:flex;font-size:10pt;margin-top:4.5pt;justify-content:flex-start;font-family:Arial;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;min-width:3.333%;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:3.5356267702001714%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#8226;</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Microsoft 365 cloud revenue increased $15.7 billion or 19% driven by Microsoft 365 commercial cloud. Microsoft 365 commercial cloud revenue increased 18% with growth in revenue per user driven by Microsoft 365 Copilot and Microsoft 365 E5. Microsoft 365 commercial seats grew 7% driven by small and medium businesses and frontline worker offerings. Microsoft 365 consumer cloud revenue increased 28% driven by growth in revenue per user and Microsoft 365 consumer subscriber growth of 7%.</span></div></div><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="margin-left:5.731%;tab-size:32px;display:flex;font-size:10pt;margin-top:4.5pt;justify-content:flex-start;font-family:Arial;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;min-width:3.333%;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:3.5356267702001714%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#8226;</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Productivity and server licensing revenue increased $1.9 billion or 5% driven by Microsoft 365 commercial products. </span></div></div><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="margin-left:5.731%;tab-size:32px;display:flex;font-size:10pt;margin-top:4.5pt;justify-content:flex-start;font-family:Arial;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;min-width:3.333%;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:3.5356267702001714%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#8226;</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Industry solutions revenue increased $1.9 billion or 10% driven by growth in Industry solutions cloud. Industry solutions cloud revenue increased 12% driven by Dynamics 365 with growth across all workloads.</span></div></div><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="margin-left:5.731%;tab-size:32px;display:flex;font-size:10pt;margin-top:4.5pt;justify-content:flex-start;font-family:Arial;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;min-width:3.333%;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:3.5356267702001714%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#8226;</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Frontier and support services revenue increased $500 million or 6% driven by growth in Customer Success Support (formerly Enterprise Support Services).</span></div></div><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:9pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Operating income increased $25.6 billion or 23%.</span></p><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="margin-left:5.731%;tab-size:32px;display:flex;font-size:10pt;margin-top:4.5pt;justify-content:flex-start;font-family:Arial;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;min-width:3.333%;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:3.5356267702001714%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#8226;</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Cost of revenue increased $20.1 billion or 33% driven by investments in AI infrastructure to support growing customer demand and Microsoft 365 Copilot seat and usage growth.</span></div></div><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="margin-left:5.731%;tab-size:32px;display:flex;font-size:10pt;margin-top:4.5pt;justify-content:flex-start;font-family:Arial;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;min-width:3.333%;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:3.5356267702001714%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#8226;</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Gross margin increased $29.2 billion or 19% driven by growth in Azure and Microsoft 365 commercial cloud. Gross margin percentage decreased driven by continued investments in AI infrastructure and growing AI product usage, offset in part by efficiency gains in Azure and Microsoft 365 commercial cloud.</span></div></div><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="margin-left:5.731%;tab-size:32px;display:flex;font-size:10pt;margin-top:4.5pt;justify-content:flex-start;font-family:Arial;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;min-width:3.333%;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:3.5356267702001714%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#8226;</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Operating expenses increased $3.7 billion or 8% driven by continued investments in research and development compute capacity, AI talent, and data to support product development that benefits the entire portfolio, as well as investments in commercial sales and higher Copilot advertising expenses.</span></div></div><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:9pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Revenue, gross margin, and operating income each included a favorable foreign currency impact of 2%.</span></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:13.5pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-style:italic;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Devices and Consumer</span></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:9pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Revenue increased $771 million or 1%.</span></p><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="margin-left:5.731%;tab-size:32px;display:flex;font-size:10pt;margin-top:4.5pt;justify-content:flex-start;font-family:Arial;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;min-width:3.333%;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:3.5356267702001714%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#8226;</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Search and advertising revenue increased $2.7 billion or 12%. Search and advertising revenue excluding traffic acquisition costs increased 14% driven by higher rate and volume across LinkedIn, Edge, and Bing.</span></div></div><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="margin-left:5.731%;tab-size:32px;display:flex;font-size:10pt;margin-top:4.5pt;justify-content:flex-start;font-family:Arial;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;min-width:3.333%;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:3.5356267702001714%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#8226;</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">XBOX revenue decreased $1.7 billion or 7% driven by declines in XBOX content and services and XBOX hardware. XBOX content and services revenue decreased 5% on a prior year comparable that benefited from strong first-party content performance, offset in part by growth in XBOX Game Pass. XBOX hardware revenue decreased 29% driven by lower volume of consoles sold. </span></div></div><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="margin-left:5.731%;tab-size:32px;display:flex;font-size:10pt;margin-top:4.5pt;justify-content:flex-start;font-family:Arial;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;min-width:3.333%;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:3.5356267702001714%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#8226;</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Windows OEM and devices revenue decreased $228 million or 1% driven by a decline in devices, offset in part by Windows OEM growth of 3% with inventory levels that remained elevated.</span></div></div><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:9pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Operating income increased $1.2 billion or 7%.</span></p><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="margin-left:5.731%;tab-size:32px;display:flex;font-size:10pt;margin-top:4.5pt;justify-content:flex-start;font-family:Arial;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;min-width:3.333%;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:3.5356267702001714%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#8226;</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Cost of revenue decreased $1.6 billion or 6% driven by lower hardware sales.</span></div></div><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="margin-left:5.731%;tab-size:32px;display:flex;font-size:10pt;margin-top:4.5pt;justify-content:flex-start;font-family:Arial;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;min-width:3.333%;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:3.5356267702001714%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#8226;</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Gross margin increased $2.4 billion or 6% driven by growth in Search and advertising and Windows OEM. Gross margin percentage increased driven by sales mix shift to higher margin businesses.</span></div></div><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="margin-left:5.731%;tab-size:32px;display:flex;font-size:10pt;margin-top:4.5pt;justify-content:flex-start;font-family:Arial;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;min-width:3.333%;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:3.5356267702001714%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#8226;</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Operating expenses increased $1.2 billion or 6% driven by impairment and other related expenses in our XBOX business and continued investments in research and development compute capacity, AI talent, and data to support product development that benefits the entire portfolio</span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-style:italic;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">.</span></div></div></div>
