  <div class="main-content-container" style="z-index:5;position:relative;"><div><ix:continuation id="F_cb8b67ec-422c-42c7-9787-31179f7eb2aa_3" continuedAt="F_cb8b67ec-422c-42c7-9787-31179f7eb2aa_4"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:9pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">As of June 30, 2026, we had federal, state, and foreign net operating loss carryforwards of $</span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"><ix:nonFraction id="F_094260fa-665c-42aa-a862-49b9b2403cda" contextRef="C_e08c01e0-cf3b-4821-a03f-bf064e800406" name="us-gaap:OperatingLossCarryforwards" unitRef="U_USD" scale="6" decimals="-6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">369</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> million, $</span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"><ix:nonFraction id="F_fb4a28ca-0ee1-4dce-831e-beb0ae68890e" contextRef="C_ef5d9fcf-3b38-4ebb-a8b5-6ed40c35c41d" name="us-gaap:OperatingLossCarryforwards" unitRef="U_USD" scale="6" decimals="-6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">715</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> million, and $</span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"><ix:nonFraction id="F_e13e86a9-6d99-4c2b-974f-7d572b72b2b7" contextRef="C_f82a2a3a-753e-48a4-bbbf-8399ec74cab2" name="us-gaap:OperatingLossCarryforwards" unitRef="U_USD" scale="9" decimals="-8" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">2.9</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> billion, respectively. The federal and state net operating loss carryforwards have varying expiration dates ranging from fiscal year </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;"><ix:nonNumeric id="F_1afd60bb-ea65-4641-9229-e53399b956c5" contextRef="C_45876a5f-7189-41e2-934a-2fbdfe7ffcd9" name="msft:OperatingLossCarryforwardsExpirationYear"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">2027</span></ix:nonNumeric></span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> to </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;"><ix:nonNumeric id="F_ec3a2847-0318-4474-831d-2f51fabce1d9" contextRef="C_2d94cfee-cee7-4b3c-8a7b-f4ddac4ab2f2" name="msft:OperatingLossCarryforwardsExpirationYear"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">2046</span></ix:nonNumeric></span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> or indefinite carryforward periods, if not utilized. The majority of our foreign net operating loss carryforwards do not expire. Certain acquired net operating loss carryforwards are subject to an annual limitation but are expected to be realized with the exception of those which have a valuation allowance. As of June 30, 2026, we had $</span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"><ix:nonFraction id="F_f9e46a7d-3da7-4d4b-99c3-83b542d73116" contextRef="C_e08c01e0-cf3b-4821-a03f-bf064e800406" name="msft:CapitalLossCarryforwards" unitRef="U_USD" scale="6" decimals="-6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">613</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> million federal capital loss carryforwards for U.S. tax purposes. The federal capital loss carryforwards will expire in fiscal year </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;"><ix:nonNumeric id="F_5ec2c8f7-4a95-4f0d-b61d-efa7d4a05432" contextRef="C_4dc742fa-8de5-4fac-8e2d-271ac6787487" name="msft:CapitalLossCarryforwardsExpirationYear"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">2030</span></ix:nonNumeric></span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> if not utilized.</span></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:9pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">The valuation allowance disclosed in the table above relates to the foreign net operating loss carryforwards, federal capital loss carryforwards, and foreign tax credits carryforwards that may not be realized.</span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> </span></p><div style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;"><ix:nonNumeric id="F_ac012f45-b191-4f7d-8c26-913d52fedc16" contextRef="C_cc83aaed-4c2b-47e2-a694-c8c5f5fe3b56" name="us-gaap:ScheduleOfCashFlowSupplementalDisclosuresTableTextBlock" escape="true"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:9pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Income taxes paid, net of refunds, pursuant to the disclosure requirements of ASU 2023-09 in fiscal year 2026 were as follows:</span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> </span></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:9pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:9pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</span></p>
