al years 2026, 2025, and 2024, respectively.</span></p></ix:nonNumeric></div><div><ix:continuation id="F_9f79a657-5ca7-470e-9ca4-706614ac7f6a_1"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:9pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Assets are not allocated to segments for internal reporting presentations. A portion of amortization and depreciation is included with various other costs in an overhead allocation to each segment. It is impracticable for us to separately identify the amount of amortization and depreciation by segment that is included in the measure of segment profit or loss.</span></p></ix:continuation></div><div style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;"><ix:nonNumeric id="F_c8d56372-90cb-4340-bb6a-a29aee4ae02a" contextRef="C_cc83aaed-4c2b-47e2-a694-c8c5f5fe3b56" name="us-gaap:LongLivedAssetsByGeographicAreasTableTextBlock" escape="true" continuedAt="F_c8d56372-90cb-4340-bb6a-a29aee4ae02a_1"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:9pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Long-lived assets, excluding financial instruments and tax assets, classified by the location of the controlling statutory company and with countries over 10% of the total shown separately, were as follows:</span></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:9pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:9pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</span></p>
